            <ArticleTitle>Penetrating atherosclerotic ulcer of the ascending aorta: the role of computed tomography scan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>671-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e32834806cd</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asymptomatic penetrating atherosclerotic ulcer is a rare pathology of the ascending aorta, more frequent in the descending thoracic aorta, even in multiple localizations. We present a case report of a patient with penetrating atherosclerotic ulcer and the preoperative role of the computed tomography scan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
